     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Family visiting and wanting things settled before rounds aren't clinical reasons for 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen. That is twice the maximum daily dose, and each 1,600 mg dose is twice the usual maximum single dose. It carries a real risk of serious GI bleeding and kidney injury, and the order would reach the patient without a safeguard.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- **Enter a dose within limits.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or 600 mg PO every 6 hours.\n- **Add a note for pharmacy or the team.** I can add a note to a standard-dose order, such as \"request pharmacy review for escalation.\"\n- **Support a documented override.** If there is a clinical reason for exceeding the limit, it should go through pharmacy or the attending. They can approve it and document it through the proper channel. I can enter the order after that.\n\nWould you like me to enter one of the within-limit options now so the patient's pain control isn't delayed?"
      }
     ],
